.TH PATH_RELATIVE 3
.SH NAME
path_relative \- compute a relative path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "int path_relative(const char* " path ", stralloc* " out ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_relative
attempts to convert an absolute or complex path into a relative path representation and appends the result to the
.B stralloc
pointed to by
.IR out .
.PP
The function parses the input
.I path
(assumed to be a null-terminated string) and resolves it relative to the current working directory or the implied structure of the provided path, depending on the implementation details and environment context.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 1 on success, or 0 if the path could not be converted to a relative form or an error occurred.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR path_append (3),
.BR path_normalize (3)